{
  "task_id": "taxonomy-tree-merge",
  "top_k": 5,
  "requirements": [
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_160d95ad91f9c7025545",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/taxonomy-tree-merge/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 1,
        "line_end": 1,
        "exact_text": "I need to unify product category taxonomies from three different e-commerce platforms (Amazon, Facebook, and Google Shopping). Each platform has its own way of classifying products, and we want to create one unified category catalog that works for all of them such that I can use one single category system for downstream works like tracking metrics of product category from multiple platforms!\n",
        "source_sha256": "f76f0d3ab731ebc65b7d7761e3bc3591dc7efbf159933be2c178319c9cee6ba9",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_7ef231209de7b84a4cdf",
      "requirement_type": "FORMAT",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/taxonomy-tree-merge/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 4,
        "line_end": 4,
        "exact_text": "- amazon_product_categories.csv\n",
        "source_sha256": "f76f0d3ab731ebc65b7d7761e3bc3591dc7efbf159933be2c178319c9cee6ba9",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_833bee1490b8f6811f58",
      "requirement_type": "FORMAT",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/taxonomy-tree-merge/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 5,
        "line_end": 5,
        "exact_text": "- fb_product_categories.csv  \n",
        "source_sha256": "f76f0d3ab731ebc65b7d7761e3bc3591dc7efbf159933be2c178319c9cee6ba9",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_362a7184a9f59193fff5",
      "requirement_type": "FORMAT",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/taxonomy-tree-merge/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 6,
        "line_end": 7,
        "exact_text": "- google_shopping_product_categories.csv\n\n",
        "source_sha256": "f76f0d3ab731ebc65b7d7761e3bc3591dc7efbf159933be2c178319c9cee6ba9",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_ffeb39fb0eb9a07e45fd",
      "requirement_type": "FORMAT",
      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/taxonomy-tree-merge/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 8,
        "line_end": 8,
        "exact_text": "Each file has different formats but all contain hierarchical category paths in format like `\"electronics > computers > Laptops\"` under the `category_path` column. Your job is to process these files and create a unified 5-level taxonomy.\n",
        "source_sha256": "f76f0d3ab731ebc65b7d7761e3bc3591dc7efbf159933be2c178319c9cee6ba9",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_d2c94e58b504ac96330e",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/taxonomy-tree-merge/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 11,
        "line_end": 11,
        "exact_text": " 1. the top level should have 10-20 broad categories, and each deeper level should have 3-20 subcategories per parent.\n",
        "source_sha256": "f76f0d3ab731ebc65b7d7761e3bc3591dc7efbf159933be2c178319c9cee6ba9",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_05ac68598122ff54068b",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/taxonomy-tree-merge/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 12,
        "line_end": 12,
        "exact_text": " 2. you should give name to category based on the available category names, use \" | \" as separator between words (not more than 5 words), and one category needs to be representative enough (70%+) of its subcategories\n",
        "source_sha256": "f76f0d3ab731ebc65b7d7761e3bc3591dc7efbf159933be2c178319c9cee6ba9",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_62622c2636a7b0d0a25b",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/taxonomy-tree-merge/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 13,
        "line_end": 13,
        "exact_text": " 3. standardize category text as much as possible\n",
        "source_sha256": "f76f0d3ab731ebc65b7d7761e3bc3591dc7efbf159933be2c178319c9cee6ba9",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_77e07d660fd3f5eb5b91",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/taxonomy-tree-merge/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 14,
        "line_end": 14,
        "exact_text": " 4. avoid name overlap between subcategory and its parent\n",
        "source_sha256": "f76f0d3ab731ebc65b7d7761e3bc3591dc7efbf159933be2c178319c9cee6ba9",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_ad53ba0021584367660e",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/taxonomy-tree-merge/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 15,
        "line_end": 15,
        "exact_text": " 5. for sibling categories, they should be distinct from each other with < 30% word overlap\n",
        "source_sha256": "f76f0d3ab731ebc65b7d7761e3bc3591dc7efbf159933be2c178319c9cee6ba9",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_ec2d61bf093da1a96050",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/taxonomy-tree-merge/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 16,
        "line_end": 16,
        "exact_text": " 6. try to balance the cluster sizes across different hierarchy levels to form a reasonable pyramid structure\n",
        "source_sha256": "f76f0d3ab731ebc65b7d7761e3bc3591dc7efbf159933be2c178319c9cee6ba9",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_f3ccb8855c5faadd16f8",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/taxonomy-tree-merge/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 17,
        "line_end": 18,
        "exact_text": " 7. ensure categories from different data sources are relatively evenly distributed across the unified taxonomy\n\n",
        "source_sha256": "f76f0d3ab731ebc65b7d7761e3bc3591dc7efbf159933be2c178319c9cee6ba9",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_b4247020a630d398f860",
      "requirement_type": "OUTPUT_PATH",
      "criticality": "HARD",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/taxonomy-tree-merge/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 19,
        "line_end": 19,
        "exact_text": "Output two CSV files to `/root/output/`:\n",
        "source_sha256": "f76f0d3ab731ebc65b7d7761e3bc3591dc7efbf159933be2c178319c9cee6ba9",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_7e3dd7e3e9c1249ff238",
      "requirement_type": "FORMAT",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/taxonomy-tree-merge/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 21,
        "line_end": 26,
        "exact_text": "1. `unified_taxonomy_full.csv`\n   - source (amazon/facebook/google)\n   - category_path\n   - depth (1-5)\n   - unified_level_1, unified_level_2, unified_level_3, unified_level_4, unified_level_5\n\n",
        "source_sha256": "f76f0d3ab731ebc65b7d7761e3bc3591dc7efbf159933be2c178319c9cee6ba9",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
